ion, very good leadership, sometimes not good at taking criticism, can be unorganized. B can be grumpy, uncooperative. C can make correct decisions quickly, difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric, not willing to further education, 100% reliable, creates positive atmosphere with crew. D responds to unexpected events adequately, can concentrate, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously, regarded as arrogant, relatively weak leadership.\n\nSarah should maybe note that Candidate C is 100% reliable and creates positive atmosphere, but communication issues and egocentric. Candidate D takes responsibility seriously, solves problems, but arrogant and weak leadership. She may argue B still best overall.\n\nThus produce public message: \"I agree with Emily's recommendation for Candidate B because ...\". Provide evidence. Vote Candidate B.\n\nProceed."}
