isis, understands complicated tech, difficulty communicating, egocentric, not willing to further education. D: responsibility, problem solving, concentration, responds to unexpected events, but arrogant, weak leadership, hot temper, know-it-all.\n\nWe need to discuss maybe candidate C's strengths: reliability, crew atmosphere, decision quality, calmness, technical competence. But communication issues. Compare with B's crew cooperation issues. Which is more severe? Need to decide if B still best.\n\nWe could argue that C's reliability and calmness are strong, and his communication difficulty is less severe than B's grumpy/uncooperative behavior. But C is egocentric, not willing to further education, difficulty communicating ideas. Might affect crew cooperation heavily.\n\nWe could also bring up D's responsibility and problem solving, but hot temper and arrogance may be severe.\n\nWe could bring up A's leadership and anticipation, but unorganized and not open to new ideas.\n\nThus B still seems best overall, but we need to address crew cooperation concerns. Perhaps propose mitigation: crew resource training.\n\nThus James should state his recommendation for B, acknowledging concerns, and perhaps suggest that B's issues are manageable compared to others.\n\nWe should reference Sarah's observation about B's grumpy/uncooperative behavior, and Emily's lack of memory info. Also reference other candidates' concerns.\n\nThus final public message: I still recommend B, because his reliability, stress resilience, technical competence outweigh crew cooperation concerns, which are less severe than egocentric or hot temper of others.\n\nVote: Candidate B.\n\nProceed."}
