ner, arrogant, weak leadership.\n\nWe need to discuss adaptability/feedback orientation, a key criterion still unclear. Since we have no direct evidence for B, but we have concerns about his uncooperative behavior, perhaps we should compare with others.\n\nCandidate A: \"struggles with criticism\" and \"not open to new ideas\" \u2013 indicates poor feedback orientation. Candidate C: \"not very willing to further his education\" \u2013 suggests low adaptability. Candidate D: \"considered moody\" and \"loner\" \u2013 may affect adaptability and feedback.\n\nThus all candidates have issues. B's issues are similar but perhaps less severe. So we might still recommend B, but note that lack of direct evidence on adaptability is a gap, but other candidates have stronger evidence of poor adaptability.\n\nThus Emily should state she still recommends B, acknowledging the gap but noting that other candidates have more serious adaptability concerns.\n\nMake sure to reference Sarah's answer and prior discussion.\n\nProceed to output PUBLIC_MESSAGE and METADATA_JSON."}
